WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.317
Basak, Lapu-Lapu City.

00:00:01.317 --> 00:00:03.353
Five households, the same stories.

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:05.927
A student revises until one in the morning;

00:00:05.927 --> 00:00:11.075
the suspension was posted at ten forty at night, on a page the family does not follow.

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:11.914
A mother says:

00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:12.931
ligo na mo karon.

00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:18.739
The water cut was announced the night before, so the drum gets filled and everyone showers early.

00:00:18.739 --> 00:00:21.852
Another family lost power and the pump in one night:

00:00:21.852 --> 00:00:24.606
spoiled food, no shower, a late start at work.

00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:27.120
And a hot afternoon with nothing prepared.

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:29.992
This is where the notices live.

00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:32.351
MECO posts brownouts as images.

00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:36.536
MCWD posts water cuts under a news tab on its own site.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.971
DepEd's memos are PDF downloads.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:42.243
PAGASA is a fourth site in a fourth format.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.718
Two facts make this worse.

00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:50.129
Since DepEd Order 22 of 2024, brownout and heat suspensions are no longer automatic:

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:52.835
the mayor decides, so the post comes late.

00:00:52.835 --> 00:00:54.896
And power and water are coupled:

00:00:54.896 --> 00:01:00.114
when the grid drops, MCWD's 147 pumps stop too, with one to two hours of warning.

00:01:00.114 --> 00:01:04.043
A notice as an image in a feed is not a record you can check.

00:01:04.643 --> 00:01:08.960
Abiso reads every official notice once and turns it into an event.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.577
This is the live prototype on Cloud Run.

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:16.483
338 disruption events from 201 official posts, refreshed every three hours.

00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:17.464
Today in Basak:

00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:23.743
an MCWD water interruption for a mainline leak repair, with the link to the notice it came from.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.255
Most people here do not search.

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:30.819
They ask.

00:01:30.819 --> 00:01:33.265
Naay water interruption sa Basak karon?

00:01:33.265 --> 00:01:42.925
The question goes to a Gemini agent built with Google's Agent Development Kit, which hands it to a water specialist that can only read the stored notices.

00:01:42.925 --> 00:01:46.250
The answer comes back in Cebuano, with the MCWD link.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:55.059
Here is the same question in the ADK developer UI.

00:01:55.059 --> 00:01:57.029
Event two is the tool call:

00:01:57.029 --> 00:01:58.999
water, Basak, today's date.

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:01.408
Event three is the tool's result.

00:02:01.408 --> 00:02:03.159
Event four is the reply.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:13.157
In the trace you can see the coordinator call Gemini, hand off to the water agent, and the water agent call the water interruptions tool.

00:02:13.157 --> 00:02:15.200
No step answers from memory.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.316
The web page is a front.

00:02:17.316 --> 00:02:19.992
The real place is the family group chat.

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:22.468
Ate Jen asks if there is still water.

00:02:22.468 --> 00:02:28.490
Mama tags Abiso, and the reply is the live answer from the same agent, with the same link.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.363
Papa says fill the drum now.

00:02:30.363 --> 00:02:37.322
Then Kuya Migs forwards a MECO poster, and Abiso reads the image and answers with the event it compiled.

00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:38.727
The webhook is built;

00:02:38.727 --> 00:02:41.470
public access waits on Meta's app review.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.501
May pasok ba bukas sa Lapu-Lapu?

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.845
There is no official notice, so Abiso says exactly that.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:03.010
A wrong answer about classes is worse than no answer.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.236
Notices change.

00:03:16.236 --> 00:03:19.721
A MECO poster announces a line fault in Pajac Agora;

00:03:19.721 --> 00:03:22.537
the next day's poster says it is resolved.

00:03:22.537 --> 00:03:27.162
In Firestore that is one event with two source posts, not two events.

00:03:27.162 --> 00:03:30.380
Extensions and cancellations merge the same way.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.443
Under the hood it is a press.

00:03:33.443 --> 00:03:39.010
Every three hours Cloud Scheduler calls the service with the new posts.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.419
Gemini 3.8 Flash on Vertex AI stamps each one once into a typed card:

00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:47.868
type, barangays, start, end, status, source.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:52.180
The card drops into its barangay's drawer in Firestore.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.767
Four doors read the same drawers:

00:03:54.767 --> 00:04:00.569
the page, the group chat, the calendar, and other agents over MCP and A2A.

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:02.607
One model call per notice;

00:04:02.607 --> 00:04:04.410
questions cost nothing.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.527
We measured it on fifty posts locked before any model saw them.

00:04:08.527 --> 00:04:16.228
Gemini got the type right every time, the start within an hour ninety two percent of the time, and barangays with ninety four percent overlap.

00:04:16.228 --> 00:04:18.560
Status is the weakest field, and we say so.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:19.846
Abiso.

00:04:19.846 --> 00:04:26.089
Official notices for Lapu-Lapu City, compiled once, answered where people already are.

00:04:26.089 --> 00:04:28.920
It is live now, and the code is public.

